{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/192074-questions-elemental-mastery-weaknesses-and-disrupt","id":192074,"title":"questions: Elemental mastery, Weaknesses and Disrupt","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-08T23:05:46-07:00","id":192074,"title":"questions: Elemental mastery, Weaknesses and Disrupt","content":"i got a player who wants to pull out an Avatar the last airbender by being able to manipulate, Water, Air and Electricity all in one package... should he buy elemental mastery 4 times? or he can only dominate one element?.<br /> <br /> I was reading that novas are sort of weak to energies such as electricity, how does this energy affects a nova if he is inmune to it? what other weaknesses do novas get?<br /> <br /> One of my players is very interested in basically go around using Disrupt constantly in order to have the upper hand over any character she meets (basically, she wants to be the game troll). How do you contrarest this? how can you turn the tables to a power such as disrupt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T23:25:21-07:00","id":192095,"title":"","content":"I'm fighting my sleep medicine to type this, so forgive it if it makes no sense. 1. Yes, he can purchase those multiple times, each for a different element. 2. Hadn't ever read that. Nova weaknesses are very individualistic, and vary one to another. 3.you could Disrupt her disrupt first. Or, let her disrupt a big guy's powers, then let her realize that Disrupt cannot Disrupt Mega Attributes, only powers. Then she gets punched in the face with Mega Strength 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T15:07:58-07:00","id":192798,"title":"","content":"Technically, yes he can buy multiple variations of Elemental Mastery, but that would get pricey.<br /> <br /> Given his character theme is apparently Avatar the Last Airbender, I'd personally recommend giving him a discount on the different Elemental Masteries.<br /> <br /> Like lustral_star mentioned, I can't recall Nova's being inherently weak to electricity. Not unless they're made of water or something.<br /> <br /> As for the Disrupt power. Well, you could have it so she's got it on permanently as an aura or something, disrupting all Nova powers around her, even the ones she'd rather not disrupt like Healers. To counter her, remember that Disrupt doesn't work on Mega Attributes and that getting punched in the face by someone with Mega Strength 5 <i>really</i> hurts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T22:14:22-07:00","id":193137,"title":"","content":"Something I didn't mention the first time: If a nova is immune to electricity, then they're <i>immune</i> to it. It won't hurt them or affect them. The most common thing I could think of to produce an effect like this would be Invulnerability: Electricity. Even then, it could still be mechanically possible for that nova to encounter an amount of electricity significant enough to overcome the extra soak provided by Invulnerability -- in which case, it affects them just the same as everyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T22:14:54-07:00","id":193151,"title":"","content":"You know, like a toad that gets struck by lightning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}